{
  "manufacturer": "Yaskawa",
  "manufacturer_slug": "yaskawa",
  "model": "J1000 compact V/f drive (MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "j1000",
  "short_model": "J1000",
  "aliases": [
    "CIMR-JU",
    "CIMR-JC",
    "J1000 Compact V/f Control Drive"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa J1000 drives (CIMR-JU/JC) with the optional RS-422/485 MEMOBUS/Modbus interface, per Technical Manual SIEP C710606 31D.",
  "summary": "The J1000 is Yaskawa's compact V/f drive; MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU needs the optional RS-422/485 interface. Commands are written to hex registers 0001H-000FH, status, fault and alarm words are read from 0020H upward, U monitors from 0040H, and parameters have their own hex addresses. This map covers the command block, all status/fault/alarm/CPF words, the main monitors, fault and alarm code tables, and the b1/H5 setup parameters.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and sent unchanged: the 03H example reads from 00 20 (drive status) and the 10H example writes 0001H/0002H from 00 01 (0002H = 1770H = 6000 for 60.00 Hz). The parameter table lists addresses in hex without the H suffix (b1-01 = 180, H5-01 = 425, U1-01 = 40)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive J1000 Compact V/f Control Drive Technical Manual",
    "doc_number": "SIEP C710606 31D",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=SIEPC71060631&cmd=documents&documentName=SIEPC71060631.pdf",
    "pages": "Appendix C pp. 217-219 (H5), p. 220 (b1), pp. 224-225 (examples), pp. 226-232 (data table, fault/alarm codes), p. 233 (Enter); parameter table pp. 198-199 (H5), 203-205 (U monitors)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "U1-03 output current reads 8192 = 100 % of drive rated current over Modbus (parameter-table footnote), so it is mapped as percent.",
    "The 10H example writes 1770H (6000) for 60.00 Hz, while H5-13 default 0 is printed as 0.1 Hz/1; because of that conflict the frequency registers are left unscaled.",
    "Left out because the sign or unit is not stated: 0007H AM output setting, 0026H output current (no unit printed), 003FH/00B6H/00B8H frequency in 0.01 % (sign not stated), 0068H heatsink temperature, 00ABH rated current, U4-06/U4-07 and U4-13.",
    "Fault and alarm values are the hex codes of Tables C.4 and C.5 converted to decimal (e.g. 0021H CE = 33).",
    "Function codes 03H, 08H and 10H only; there is no single-register write (06H). Up to 16 registers per message.",
    "Broadcast (address 0) accepts 0001H (bit 0 run, bit 1 direction, bit 4 external fault, bit 5 fault reset, bit C S5) and 0002H (30000 = 100 %)."
  ],
